1
00:00:00,022 --> 00:00:01,817
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,983 --> 00:00:05,895
In this lesson, we will put the right
resgrid app on each device.

3
00:00:06,112 --> 00:00:09,761
A configured department still needs
members and shared devices

4
00:00:09,772 --> 00:00:13,279
to sign in to the correct department with
the correct permissions.

5
00:00:13,458 --> 00:00:17,175
We will explain the features, the setup
decisions, and a

6
00:00:17,175 --> 00:00:19,282
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:20,092 --> 00:00:22,192
Members install the Responder app,

8
00:00:22,381 --> 00:00:27,149
a tablet in Engine 1 runs the Unit app and
a station screen shows the Big Board.

9
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:30,339
Most members use Resgrid through the
Responder app.

10
00:00:30,555 --> 00:00:34,708
Getting everyone installed and signed in
is what lets dispatches reach them.

11
00:00:34,873 --> 00:00:38,846
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:38,846 --> 00:00:41,290
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:42,116 --> 00:00:46,318
Responder application. The member app for
receiving dispatches,

14
00:00:46,489 --> 00:00:48,427
responding and setting status.

15
00:00:48,653 --> 00:00:53,571
Have every member install the Responder
app, sign in and allow notifications.

16
00:00:54,373 --> 00:00:58,795
Unit application. The in-vehicle app that
represents an apparatus.

17
00:00:58,986 --> 00:01:03,107
Install the Unit app on each apparatus
tablet and select its unit.

18
00:01:03,878 --> 00:01:08,633
Dispatch application. The dispatcher view
for creating and managing calls.

19
00:01:08,854 --> 00:01:13,319
Give dispatch access to the people who
dispatch, then have them sign in.

20
00:01:14,112 --> 00:01:16,276
Incident command and accountability.

21
00:01:16,442 --> 00:01:19,987
Incident command and accountability for
incident commanders.

22
00:01:20,208 --> 00:01:23,363
Give command access to the officers who
run incidents.

23
00:01:24,162 --> 00:01:28,430
Big Board. A station display of calls,
units and personnel.

24
00:01:28,619 --> 00:01:32,108
Open the Big Board on a station screen and
choose what it shows.

25
00:01:32,907 --> 00:01:38,540
Dashboard. The department home page:
current status, staffing and activity.

26
00:01:38,723 --> 00:01:41,981
Decide which devices each role will use
and share the app

27
00:01:41,983 --> 00:01:43,811
download links with your members.

28
00:01:44,631 --> 00:01:50,492
My Profile. Your own profile, contact
details and notification preferences.

29
00:01:50,716 --> 00:01:53,972
Decide which devices each role will use
and share the app

30
00:01:53,974 --> 00:01:55,809
download links with your members.

31
00:01:56,613 --> 00:02:00,501
Your Departments. Switch between the
departments you belong to.

32
00:02:00,702 --> 00:02:03,956
Decide which devices each role will use
and share the app

33
00:02:03,959 --> 00:02:05,785
download links with your members.

34
00:02:06,649 --> 00:02:09,521
For the training scenario, work in this
order.

35
00:02:09,744 --> 00:02:14,845
Step 1. Set up a member device with
Responder and notification permissions.

36
00:02:15,102 --> 00:02:19,635
Step 2. Set up an apparatus tablet with
Unit and select its unit.

37
00:02:19,859 --> 00:02:23,701
Step 3. Grant appropriate Dispatch or
Command access and

38
00:02:23,701 --> 00:02:25,712
configure a station Big Board.

39
00:02:26,495 --> 00:02:28,143
Now verify the result.

40
00:02:28,358 --> 00:02:31,921
Check the active department, device
identity, and a

41
00:02:31,921 --> 00:02:34,035
controlled notification test.

42
00:02:34,229 --> 00:02:36,973
Check what a shared station screen
exposes.

43
00:02:37,188 --> 00:02:41,938
A common problem to watch for: Installing
an app does not prove alerts arrive.

44
00:02:42,099 --> 00:02:47,300
Verify OS notification and location
settings on the actual device used.

45
00:02:48,079 --> 00:02:49,905
Your practice task is simple.

46
00:02:50,054 --> 00:02:55,028
Use a sample member, unit tablet,
dispatcher, and station display to

47
00:02:55,029 --> 00:02:57,028
follow the same training incident.

48
00:02:57,202 --> 00:02:59,853
Record which devices complete the test.

49
00:03:00,021 --> 00:03:04,539
Record the result, who owns the follow-up,
and when it should be reviewed.

50
00:03:04,672 --> 00:03:08,635
Use the linked feature scripts for the
detailed screen recording plan.

